# Integration mapping for Libretro (Console emulation)
# Format: upstream_path:goliath_path:action
# Actions: copy, copy+modify, exclude, manual

# This file tracks how upstream Libretro code maps to Goliath's integration.

## Core files (direct copy from upstream)
# Most libretro-common files are copied directly
# include/:libs/libretro/include/:copy
# features/:libs/libretro/features/:copy
# file/:libs/libretro/file/:copy
# streams/:libs/libretro/streams/:copy

## Modified files (copied but with Goliath-specific changes)
# Document any modifications here

## Excluded files (not needed for Goliath integration)
# .github/:exclude
# audio/:exclude (may not need audio mixing in core)
# net/:exclude (networking handled separately)

## Manual integration files (managed by Goliath, not synced)
# Makefile.in:manual

## Notes
# - Libretro provides common code for emulators
# - Used for console ROM support
# - Works with retroarch for actual emulation
# - We integrate the common library, not specific cores
